# Cinatra code owners.
# Listed owners are requested for review on pull requests that touch matching
# paths. Reference: https://docs.github.com/articles/about-code-owners
#
# Routing policy:
#   - Routine paths intentionally have NO code owner. They match no rule in this
#     file, so no review is auto-requested for anyone on ordinary changes.
#   - Security-relevant / supply-chain surfaces request both the owner
#     (@groganz) and the org review account (@megajustice).
#
# NOTE: CODEOWNERS governs review *routing* only. High-risk paths (defined in
# .github/gate-suite.json -> highRiskPaths, e.g. .github/**, CODEOWNERS, auth,
# migrations, release/publish) INDEPENDENTLY require a maintainer-tier approval
# enforced by the truthful-attribution-gate, regardless of this file's routing.

# Security-relevant surfaces.
# Repository automation, CI/CD definitions, and dependency manifests gate the
# supply chain and governance, so changes here request both the owner
# (@groganz) and the org review account (@megajustice).
/.github/           @groganz @megajustice
/SECURITY.md        @groganz @megajustice
/.github/workflows/ @groganz @megajustice

# CI work the maintainer commissioned on 2026-09-29 (checks that the border
# between the application and its extensions holds, and that a connector
# extension creates no artifact) changes the three workflow files below. A
# pattern without an owner unsets ownership for the files it matches, so a pull
# request that changes only these files requests and requires no code owner
# review. Every other path below /.github/ keeps the owners named above. The
# truthful-attribution-gate still classes all of /.github/ as high-risk. These
# rows are removed again once the commissioned work has merged (cinatra#3823).
/.github/workflows/gates.yml
/.github/workflows/extension-conformance-gate.yml
/.github/workflows/extension-conformance-gate-reusable.yml

# Public project metadata (licensing).
/LICENSE            @groganz @megajustice
